[=#oracleverifiertype]
= Password Verifier Type =

The //verifiertype// option sets which kind of password verifier the Oracle protocol module tells clients it uses: 9i, 11g or 12c.  If unset, it follows //serverversion// (see [oracleprotoserverversion.html Server Version]): 12c for 12.1, and 11g for 11.2.  Any other value is the same as leaving it out.

{{{#!blockquote
{{{#!code
@parts/sqlrelay-oraclefeverifiertype.conf@
}}}
}}}

Clients older than Oracle 10g, such as OCI7 apps, can only log in with 9i, and modern clients can't log in with it.  9i also makes the module report Oracle 10.2, whatever //serverversion// says.  It is much less secure than the others, so only use it for clients that need it.  A 9i listener can share an instance, and its back-end database, with a modern one.  Just give it its own port, as shown below.

{{{#!blockquote
{{{#!code
@parts/sqlrelay-oraclefeverifiertype9i.conf@
}}}
}}}

----

